# SES Product Conventions

- This repo is a **product**, not the SES kit. Install the toolkit with `pip install ses-cli`.
- After clone: `pip install ses-cli && ses setup` (add `--docs` for `.ses/standards/`).
- Commit product truth: app source, `ses.toml`, `.env.example`, your `docs/`. Gitignore regenerable SES Cursor files (see `.gitignore`); restore with `ses setup`.
- Run `ses check` from the product root when `ses.toml` exists.
- Secrets only in `.env` (gitignored). Never commit secrets.
- Tiny ≠ normal ≠ sensitive — see standards (via `ses setup --docs` or the kit).
- Do not create cloud resources or touch production without explicit human approval.
